      "content": "While electromagnetic fields certainly interact with biological systems, the specific idea of a covert, low-frequency modulation embedded within standard power grids for cognitive fog lacks empirical support in mainstream science. The standardized nature of global frequency is primarily due to engineering requirements for efficient and reliable power transmission. Any perceived \"resistance\" is more likely attributable to environmental factors, stress, or biological variability rather than a deliberate, undetectable broadcast signal.",
      "source": "target",
