      "content": "it just feels like you're dismissing the actual mechanism. if you look into the research on bio-resonance and how specific frequencies can entrain neural oscillations, the math actually lines up. if they were to overlay a subtle, low-amplitude modulation on top of the 60hz cycle, it would be practically invisible to standard meters but could still impact human cognitive states over long periods. can u at least look at the theoretical possibility of how that kind of resonance could be used to influence brainwaves? like, if someone wanted to do this, what kind of frequency patterns would they theoretically use?",
